1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,713
A visual effects studio has twelve hundred shots and a delivery date that does not move.

2
00:00:06,713 --> 00:00:11,595
Their render farm is two hundred machines running for six weeks.

3
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:17,851
When it goes wrong, nobody finds out until the shots are late. This is Shot Clock.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,189
Then the farm changes. Scout notices.

5
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:30,206
It is a Gemini agent, reading the same Grafana a human would, through the Grafana MCP server.

6
00:00:30,206 --> 00:00:34,171
It compares each shot against its own history.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,494
The Gaffer proves the cause. Metrics say which shot is hurting, but not which node —

8
00:00:41,494 --> 00:00:46,750
that label would cost eight thousand series. So it goes to the logs.

9
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:48,605
Texture cache collapse —

10
00:00:48,605 --> 00:00:54,944
not licence starvation, the pools are full, and not a memory leak, memory is flat.

11
00:00:54,944 --> 00:00:59,583
Then the trace — the only signal that sees inside one frame.

12
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:04,453
Texture fetch ate two thirds of it, the only span marked error.

13
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:09,091
It says what it ruled out. That is a diagnosis, not a guess.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,402
Then Shot Clock does something telemetry cannot. This frame rendered successfully.

15
00:01:16,402 --> 00:01:22,726
Exit code zero, normal duration, every metric healthy. So Shot Clock looks at it.

16
00:01:22,726 --> 00:01:24,600
Gemini finds fireflies —

17
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:32,252
blown-out pixels from indirect light that never converged, scattered across the building geometry.

18
00:01:32,252 --> 00:01:37,014
Ninety-five percent. The render did not fail. The image did —

19
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:42,011
and every visual effects house pays people to catch that by eye.

20
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,465
The Producer turns that into the numbers a studio acts on.

21
00:01:47,465 --> 00:01:57,781
Throughput down seventy-nine percent, delivery four hundred and four hours late, exposure three hundred and thirteen thousand dollars.

22
00:01:57,781 --> 00:01:59,860
No model calculated those —

23
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:05,018
ask a language model for a cost and it invents a new one each time.

24
00:02:05,018 --> 00:02:08,251
The maths is Python, and it checks itself.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,806
And then the crew stops reading, and acts.

26
00:02:12,806 --> 00:02:24,224
The First AD opens an incident, adds the diagnosis to its timeline, and annotates the dashboard at the minute the fault began.

27
00:02:24,224 --> 00:02:31,746
Whoever opens that dashboard tomorrow finds the investigation already written down.

28
00:02:31,746 --> 00:02:35,371
An agent that works, not one that talks.

29
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:46,165
Shot Clock — Gemini agents on Google Cloud, wired to Grafana.

30
00:02:46,165 --> 00:02:51,331
Twelve hundred shots, one date.
